  "configuration_id": "config_018",
  "reason": "Evidence: The best configuration so far is config_002 (RNA-only, multi-profile, PCA, avgpool) at 0.591 acc, while image-only models are very weak (0.208–0.227). Avgpool aggregation clearly outperforms transformer (0.591 vs 0.519). The critical open question is whether adding the image modality to the strong RNA signal provides any benefit, or whether the weak image features will dilute the RNA signal. Question tested: config_018 directly extends config_002 by adding ResNet50 image features with concat fusion, keeping all other design choices identical (multi-profile, PCA n2000, avgpool). This isolates the effect of introducing the image modality. Why best next experiment: It is the single most informative comparison under budget constraints—a clean A/B test of 'best RNA setup' vs 'best RNA setup + image.' The result will determine whether to invest remaining budget in multimodal fusion strategies (weighted, better image encoders) or to focus on improving the RNA-only pipeline (e.g., scvi/scgpt encoders). Concat is the simplest fusion, making it the appropriate first probe before committing to more complex fusion variants."
}

